            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "How is internal audit different from statutory audit?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Internal audit evaluates controls efficiency and risk reporting to Audit Committee. Statutory audit provides opinion on financial statements reporting to shareholders. Section 144 prohibits same person from performing both."
