    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <div class="faq-expanded">
                <aside class="faq-expanded__aside">
                    <h2 class="faq-expanded__title">FAQs: Internal Audit in Chennai</h2>
                    <p class="faq-expanded__lead">Answers to common questions about internal audit services in Chennai, covering Section 138 applicability, thresholds, and compliance.</p>
                    @include('partials.faq-enquiry-form', ['enquiryLocation' => 'Chennai', 'enquiryService' => 'Internal Audit in Chennai'])
                </aside>
                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is internal audit under Section 138?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Independent evaluation of internal controls, risk management, and operations by an appointed internal auditor - a CA, Cost Accountant, or Board-approved professional. Reports findings and recommendations to Audit Committee or Board. Scope defined by Audit Committee.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Which companies in Chennai must have internal audit?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>All listed companies, unlisted public with turnover above Rs 200 crore or capital above Rs 50 crore or borrowings above Rs 100 crore or deposits above Rs 25 crore, and private companies with turnover above Rs 200 crore or borrowings above Rs 100 crore.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Who can be appointed as internal auditor?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>A CA (practicing or non-practicing), Cost Accountant, or any professional approved by the Board. Can be employee or external firm. Statutory auditor CANNOT be internal auditor per Section 144.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the penalty for not appointing internal auditor?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Rs 10,000 for company and each defaulting officer under Section 450. If non-compliance continues, Rs 1,000 per day additional. Compoundable under Section 441. Must appoint within 6 months of crossing threshold.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How is internal audit different from statutory audit?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Internal audit evaluates controls, efficiency, and risk - reports to Audit Committee/Board. Statutory audit provides opinion on financial statements - reports to shareholders. Section 144 prohibits same person from performing both.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How often should internal audit be conducted?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Companies Act does not prescribe fixed frequency. Audit Committee determines periodicity. Common practice: quarterly with annual coverage of all key risk areas. High-risk areas may be audited more frequently.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-7">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Is internal audit mandatory for all private companies?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>No. Mandatory only for private companies with turnover above Rs 200 crore or borrowings above Rs 100 crore in preceding FY. Smaller companies can voluntarily implement for better governance.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-8">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What does an internal auditor check?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Internal financial controls, operational process efficiency, regulatory compliance (Companies Act, GST, TDS, labour laws), risk management framework, IT controls, inventory management, and any specific areas directed by the Audit Committee.</p></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>


            <!-- Quick Answers -->
            <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:32px;">
                <p><strong>Quick Answers</strong></p>
                <p><strong>Internal audit kis company ko karna padta hai?</strong> All listed companies + unlisted public (turnover Rs 200 Cr+, capital Rs 50 Cr+, loans Rs 100 Cr+, deposits Rs 25 Cr+) + private (turnover Rs 200 Cr+ ya loans Rs 100 Cr+).</p><p><strong>Statutory auditor internal audit kar sakta hai kya?</strong> Nahi. Section 144 ke under statutory auditor internal audit nahi kar sakta. Dono alag hone chahiye.</p><p><strong>Penalty kya hai non-compliance ki?</strong> Rs 10,000 + Rs 1,000/day under Section 450. Company aur defaulting officers dono par lagti hai.</p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

